  "description": "KADCEB crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C39 H39 Cl1 Ho3 N6 O13 3+,3(H2 O1),3(Cl1 1-). From the CIF bond table, Ho1 (Ho) has 6 O neighbors; Ho2 (Ho) has 7 O neighbors; Ho3 (Ho) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 3 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.530-3.551 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 96.42-98.13°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C39H45Cl4Ho3N6O16. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 5 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
